      "created_at": "2021-04-03T16:48:57Z",
      "updated_at": "2021-04-03T16:48:57Z",
      "body": "Which cookies are you referring to as being non-compliant?\r\n\r\nWith the PHP session ID cookie, I'm not sure there's anything we can do due to the nature of PHP.\r\nI don't believe it's considered to be an issue though - although if someone knows more on this than I do please do let me know.\r\n\r\nThe other cookies Nameless sets are compliant - no cookies are stored unless the user has consented to them.\r\n\r\nThird party cookies are another question, for example Google Analytics if you've added that to your site. In that case, we could maybe offer easy integration with Cookiebot which can cover these cookies.",
      "author_association": "MEMBER",
      "pin": null,
